@startuml
title Prompt Construction (prompt_builder.py)

participant "SimulationOrchestrator" as Orch
participant "PromptBuilder" as PB
participant "Agent\n(stance_history)" as Agent
participant "MemePoolManager" as MPM
participant "vision_fallback" as VF

Orch -> PB: build_discussion_prompt(agent, neighbor_posts, turn,\nemphasize_format=False)

note over Orch, PB
  neighbor_posts is list[Interaction], NOT list[Agent].
  Only Interaction carries content_type and meme_id, without
  which a neighbour's meme post cannot be rendered at all.
  The list is the frozen turn-start snapshot (Fix F).
end note

PB -> Agent: stance_history[-5:]
note right of Agent
  Fix A's memory window, counted in TURNS not tokens,
  so no language silently receives less context.
  Re-sliced here because validate_assignment cannot see
  an in-place append: this is the cap that reaches the model.
end note
Agent --> PB: up to 5 prior (turn, stance, reason)

alt turn == 1
    PB -> PB: omit the neighbour block entirely
    note right of PB: Nobody has posted yet. Showing bare initial\nstances would be a stimulus with no analogue\nin any later turn.
else turn > 1
    loop for each neighbour post
        alt content_type == "meme"
            PB -> MPM: get_meme(meme_id)
            MPM --> PB: MemeContent
            PB -> VF: build_meme_prompt(meme, receiver_supports_vision)
            note right of VF
              The ONLY place a meme-derived prompt is built.
              Duplicating its framing here would drift.
            end note
            VF --> PB: (framed text, image bytes or None)
        else content_type == "generated_text"
            PB -> PB: render "agent_id (position N): reason_text"
        end
    end
    note over PB
      At most ONE image per prompt: generate() takes a single
      image but N neighbours may include several memes. The
      first meme-bearing neighbour in (seeded, reproducible)
      order supplies it; the rest degrade to captions and set
      used_vision_fallback.
    end note
end

PB -> PB: append language directive
note right of PB
  THE RQ1 VALIDITY GUARANTEE.
  Exactly one line varies across language conditions;
  every other line is byte-identical. Measured spread
  between the three directives: 42 characters.
end note

PB -> PB: append output-format block
note right of PB
  Must satisfy stance_parser's regex. parse_stance strips
  EVERY "STANCE: <n>" occurrence from reason_text, so the
  prompt demands the line once, first, and never restated:
  a restatement would silently vanish from the field RQ2
  analyses.
  emphasize_format=True (retries 2 and 3) changes ONLY this
  block, so a retry is the same experimental stimulus.
end note

PB --> Orch: BuiltPrompt(text, image, used_vision_fallback)
Orch -> Orch: gateway.generate(text, image=image, ...)\nInteraction.used_vision_fallback = built.used_vision_fallback

@enduml
